Evaluate liquid extraction with actual partition, finite phases and solvent recovery (@ic-extraction: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-chemistry, #source "../sources/LearnChemE-Process-Self-Study.lingua#r_4KM1THP1QA2SZ5JJ9E1HSMN529", #source "../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K", #source "../sources/Speciality-Inorganic-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_04G7NFYXE76QCB3DXCRJC1FSCP", #industrial-chemistry "Adsorption-ion-exchange-membranes-and-regeneration.lingua#r_794F81FPAZEEDBSKVX4T3EHNFM") { r_78X0A79WGSPRMBEH16G2MCDN5G
**Read:** [LearnChemE — chemical-process self-study modules](../sources/LearnChemE-Process-Self-Study.lingua#r_4KM1THP1QA2SZ5JJ9E1HSMN529), the complete liquid-liquid extraction and finite-stage balance material; [Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC](../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K), the whole relevant extraction, washing, isolation and solvent-recovery treatment; [Production of Speciality Inorganic Chemicals, BREF SIC](../sources/Speciality-Inorganic-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_04G7NFYXE76QCB3DXCRJC1FSCP), the full relevant product separation and purity account.

Liquid extraction redistributes components between liquid phases. Define the distribution ratio at the actual composition, temperature, pH/speciation and solvent condition. Selectivity compares specified components under those same conditions; a large ratio for the target does not alone establish useful purification.

Finite phase inventories matter. For a dilute single-contact model with distribution ratio D=C_extract/C_raffinate, initially solute-free extractant volume V_E and raffinate volume V_R, the raffinate fraction remaining is V_R/(V_R+DV_E). Repeated fresh contacts differ from one contact with the same total solvent, and countercurrent staging has different balances again.

Real systems include mutual solubility, emulsions, entrainment, solvent degradation, phase disengagement and possible chemical reaction. Track extraction, washing, stripping and solvent recycle together. A high target recovery can carry an impurity or create an expensive regeneration/separation duty.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete extraction process using primary equilibrium, contact and recovery methods. Independently check a finite-stage benchmark, compare alternative solvent/contact arrangements and quantify impurity and solvent fate. Explain the additional evidence required when the dilute constant-distribution approximation fails or the interface becomes difficult to separate.

**Continue:** [Follow selective separations through capacity, transport, regeneration and waste](Adsorption-ion-exchange-membranes-and-regeneration.lingua#r_794F81FPAZEEDBSKVX4T3EHNFM).

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618).
